@startuml case-lifecycle
title The life of a case — who acts at each step, and what the step is for\n(the assistant proposes; only the CSR's click changes the case)

skinparam activityBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam activityBorderColor #2688D4
skinparam arrowColor #2688D4
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FCF3D0
skinparam noteBorderColor #C0A040
skinparam swimlaneBorderColor #A0A0A0

|CSR|
start
:Open a case
(**POST /api/cases**);
|Server|
:**case.open**: the case is assigned to the CSR;
note right
  Purpose: one customer matter, owned by one CSR
  (SU-1, SU-14); only the assignee acts in it.
end note

|CSR|
:Ask about an account in the chat
("Does Acme Corp have SSO?");
|Assistant|
:Find the account; propose it as the case's subject
(tool **propose_case_subject**);
|Server|
:**account.read** decision on the account (audited),
the tool result carries the name as stored;
note right
  Purpose: fix which account the case is about,
  so every question and change has one account
  context and one audit trail. Text the model
  reads never chooses it.
end note
if (May the CSR read it?) then (yes)
  :Account card with **Set as case subject**;
else (no)
  :Refused as any read (AU-6): no card,
  the case keeps no subject;
  detach
endif

|CSR|
:Click **Set as case subject**
(**PUT …/subject**);
|Server|
:**case.set-subject**: account.read on it again,
assignee check; set once (a second: 409);

|CSR|
:Look up the person on the line by email,
click **Set as contact** on their own account
(**PUT …/contact**);
|Server|
:**case.set-contact**: an individual's own account,
any earlier authentication is cleared;
note right
  Purpose: record who is asking, so a change they
  ask for is checked against what they may request
  in the account (SU-8). Identification only:
  a claim, not yet proof.
end note

|CSR|
:Ask the contact the security questions
on file, outside the system;
:Record the outcome
(**POST …/contact-authentication**, kind **Knowledge**);
|Server|
if (Passed?) then (yes)
  :**case.authenticate-contact**: kind, CSR, time recorded;
else (no)
  :409 **contact_authentication_failed**, audited;
endif
note right
  Purpose: record how sure we are that the contact
  is who they claim to be, before anything they ask
  for can change the account (grants-and-approvals).
end note

|CSR|
:Work the case in the chat;
|Assistant|
:Check, list, explain — on the subject only;
note right
  Purpose: a case stays about one account;
  only finding accounts crosses accounts.
end note
:Draft a case summary
(tool **draft_case_summary**: kept in the case agent);

|CSR|
:Review and edit the draft in the case panel,
choose a reason (**Resolved**, **Abandoned**),
click **Close case** (**POST …/closure**);
|Server|
:**case.close**, in one transaction:
pending change requests and approvals canceled
(from grants-and-approvals), the assignment ended,
the reviewed summary stored on the case;
:Open connections closed (**4404 case_unavailable**);
note right
  Purpose: nothing stays pending, and the database
  keeps what the case was about and how it ended.
  From now on the case answers 404 to everyone:
  it has no assignee (SU-14, explain-access D1).
end note
stop

@enduml
